---
const { intents, agentBrief, sourceRepo } = Astro.props;
---
      <section id="brief" class="start-hero start-stage" data-start-stage="brief">
        <div class="start-hero-copy">
          <p class="hara-v2-kicker">Repository-guided start · Optional path</p>
          <h1>Use an agent to inspect Hara before choosing an example.</h1>
          <p class="start-lede">This is one way to navigate the repository, not the definition of learning Hara. The brief asks an agent to read the named files, distinguish implemented work from prototypes or plans, propose examples grounded in source, and provide the verification command used for the selected revision.</p>

          <fieldset class="start-intent-fieldset">
            <legend>Which kind of example are you looking for?</legend>
            <div class="start-intent-grid" role="group" aria-label="Choose an example context">
              {intents.map((intent, index) => (
                <button
                  class:list={["start-intent", { "is-active": index === 0 }]}
                  type="button"
                  data-intent={intent.id}
                  data-intent-prompt={intent.prompt}
                  aria-pressed={index === 0 ? "true" : "false"}
                >
                  <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
                  {intent.label}
                </button>
              ))}
            </div>
          </fieldset>

          <div class="start-hero-actions">
            <button class="start-action start-action-primary" type="button" data-copy-agent-brief>
              <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
              Copy the repository brief
            </button>
            <a class="start-action" href={sourceRepo}>Open hara-lang/hara</a>
            <a class="start-text-link" href="#habitat">View the sample program ↓</a>
          </div>

          <div class="start-trust-strip" aria-label="Repository guide requirements">
            <div><b>Source</b><span>Name the files and revision used</span></div>
            <div><b>Status</b><span>Label implemented, prototype, or planned work</span></div>
            <div><b>Verification</b><span>Run and report the relevant command</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="start-agent-window" aria-label="Copyable repository brief">
          <div class="start-window-bar">
            <div class="start-window-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
            <span>Repository brief / hara-lang/hara</span>
            <span class="start-window-state"><i></i> Ready to copy</span>
          </div>
          <div class="start-repo-field">
            <span aria-hidden="true">⌘</span>
            <code>github.com/hara-lang/hara</code>
            <span>public repository</span>
          </div>
          <pre class="start-agent-brief" data-agent-brief tabindex="0">{agentBrief}</pre>
          <div class="start-agent-footer">
            <span>Selected context: <b data-selected-intent>make something move</b></span>
            <button type="button" data-copy-agent-brief>Copy brief</button>
          </div>
          <p class="start-agent-note"><b>Reference note.</b> This Visual Language route does not call GitHub or execute Hara. It records the expected interaction and uses a local browser simulation; repository and runtime claims must be checked against their named sources.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
